## 4. Development Commands

### Build

Desktop (default member):
```
cargo build
```

Android APK (from project root):
```
ANDROID_NDK_HOME=/path/to/ndk/27.0.12077973 \
  cargo ndk -t arm64-v8a -P 26 -o android/app/src/main/jniLibs build
cd android && gradle assembleDebug
adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
adb shell am start -n com.zdroid/.MainActivity
```

Alternatively, build from the Android example directory:
```
cd crates/gpui_android/examples/zed_android
ANDROID_NDK_HOME=/path/to/ndk/27.0.12077973 \
  cargo ndk -t arm64-v8a -P 26 -o android/app/src/main/jniLibs build
cd android && gradle assembleDebug
```

### Test

```
cargo test --workspace
cargo nextest run --workspace --no-fail-fast    # CI runner
```

### Lint

```
./script/clippy              # preferred over `cargo clippy`
cargo fmt --all -- --check
./script/prettier
typos --config typos.toml
```

### CI / Workflow Generation

```
cargo xtask workflows        # generate CI workflows (gh-workflow crate)
```

Workflows are generated from `tooling/xtask/src/tasks/workflows.rs` using the `gh-workflow` crate. There is no committed `.github/workflows/` directory — CI is external/upstream.

### Bootstrap

```
./script/bootstrap           # installs Linux/macOS dev dependencies, minio, sqlx-cli
```

## 5. Code Conventions & Common Patterns

> **`.rules` at the project root is the authoritative source for per-agent coding guidelines.** Read `.rules` every session. The following summarizes key conventions; see `.rules` for the full detail.

### Rust

- Rust 2024 edition, style_edition 2024 (see `rustfmt.toml`)
- No `mod.rs` paths — `src/some_module.rs` preferred over `src/some_module/mod.rs`
- No `unwrap()` — use `?` (error propagation) or `.log_err()` instead
- Never `let _ = ...` on fallible operations; use `?`, `.log_err()`, or explicit `match`/`if let Err(...)`
- Full word variable names (no abbreviations like `q` for `queue`)
- Variable shadowing to scope clones in async contexts (minimizing lifetime of borrowed references)
- Prefer implementing functionality in existing files; avoid many small files
- Avoid creative additions unless explicitly requested
- Prefer `[lib] path = "...rs"` in Cargo.toml for library roots (e.g., `gpui.rs`, `main.rs`)

### GPUI Patterns

- `Entity<T>` for state management, `WeakEntity<T>` for weak handles
- `cx.spawn(async move |cx| ...)` for foreground async; `cx.background_spawn(...)` for background work
- `cx.listener()` for event handlers that update the current entity
- `SharedString` for strings (either `&'static str` or `Arc<str>`)
- `cx.notify()` to trigger re-render after state changes
- `cx.emit()` / `cx.subscribe()` for entity events
- Timers in tests: use `cx.background_executor().timer(duration).await`, never `smol::Timer::after(...)`
- Element tree conditionals: `.when(condition, ...)` and `.when_some(option, ...)`

### Clippy Restrictions

From `clippy.toml`:
- `std::process::Command::spawn` / `.output` / `.status` / `.stdin` / `.stdout` / `.stderr` — use `smol::process::Command` instead
- `smol::Timer::after` in tests — replaced with `gpui::BackgroundExecutor::timer`
- `serde_json::from_reader` / `serde_json_lenient::from_reader` — use `from_slice` (buffer first)

### PR Hygiene

- Imperative title, correctly capitalized (e.g., `Fix crash in project panel`)
- No conventional commit prefixes (`fix:`, `feat:`, `docs:`)
- Optionally prefix with crate name when one crate is the clear scope (e.g., `git_ui: Add history view`)
- Mandatory `Release Notes:` section as the final section in the PR body

## 6. Major Subsystems

| Subsystem | Key crates | Purpose |
|-----------|-----------|---------|
| GPUI Framework | `gpui`, `gpui_macros`, `gpui_platform`, `gpui_android`, `gpui_wgpu`, `gpui_macos`, `gpui_linux`, `gpui_windows`, `gpui_web`, `gpui_tokio` | GPU-accelerated UI framework with platform-specific backends |
| Editor Core | `editor` | Main editor with display_map, inlays, multi-buffer, git sub-modules |
| Language System | `language`, `language_core`, `languages`, `text`, `language_extension` | Buffer management, syntax highlighting, LSP integration |
| Project System | `project`, `worktree`, `lsp`, `dap` | LSP store, git store, worktree management, debug adapters |
| Workspace & UI | `workspace`, `ui`, `ui_input`, `picker`, `component`, `sidebar` | Pane management, UI component library, panel system |
| Collaboration | `collab`, `collab_ui`, `client`, `rpc`, `proto` | Server + client RPC, WebRTC calling, channels |
| Agent / AI | `agent`, `opencode`, `prompt_store`, `agent_ui`, `agent_skills` | AI coding assistant with tools, templates, skills |
| LLM Providers | `anthropic`, `open_ai`, `google_ai`, `ollama`, `deepseek`, `mistral`, `bedrock`, `lmstudio`, `x_ai`, `open_router`, `codestral` | Per-provider API clients for LLM integration |
| Android Runtime | `gpui_android`, `zdroid_runtime` | Android platform backend (GameActivity/JNI/wgpu) + runtime adapter (bootstrap/chroot/external) |
| Terminal | `terminal`, `terminal_view` | Alacritty-based terminal emulator |
| Vim Mode | `vim`, `vim_mode_setting` | Full vim modal editing |
| Git | `git`, `git_ui`, `git_graph`, `git_hosting_providers` | Blame, diff, commit graph, hosting provider integration |
| Search | `search`, `buffer_diff` | Buffer and project-wide search, streaming diff |
| Extensions | `extension`, `extension_host`, `extension_api`, `extensions_ui`, `extension_cli` | WASM-based extension system |
| Settings | `settings`, `settings_ui`, `settings_json`, `settings_macros`, `theme`, `theme_settings` | User settings, themes, persistence |
| Debugging | `debugger_ui`, `debugger_tools`, `dap`, `dap_adapters`, `debug_adapter_extension` | Debug adapter protocol, debugger UI |
| Diagnostics | `diagnostics`, `editor` diagnostics | Error/warning squiggles, diagnostics panel |
| Audio/Video | `audio`, `call`, `livekit_api`, `livekit_client`, `denoise` | WebRTC calling, audio playback |
| Auto Update | `auto_update`, `auto_update_ui` | In-app update mechanism (desktop) |

## 7. Important Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `Cargo.toml` | Workspace definition, dependencies, member list (~230 crates) |
| `rust-toolchain.toml` | Rust 1.95.0, targets: aarch64-linux-android, wasm32-wasip2, wasm32-unknown-unknown, x86_64-unknown-linux-musl |
| `rustfmt.toml` | Edition 2024, style_edition 2024 |
| `clippy.toml` | Disallowed methods/types, interior mutability exemptions |
| `.rules` | Per-agent coding guidelines — the authoritative source, read every session |
| `.cargo/config.toml` | rustflags (v0 mangling, tokio_unstable), aliases (xtask, perf-test), Windows-specific flags |
| `.prettierrc` | printWidth 120 |
| `crates/zed/src/main.rs` | Main editor entry point |
| `crates/gpui_android/src/gpui_android.rs` | Android platform backend entry |
| `crates/zdroid_runtime/src/zdroid_runtime.rs` | Runtime adapter crate root |
| `.factory/prompts/crash/investigate.md` | Crash investigation prompts (Sentry) |
| `.factory/prompts/crash/fix.md` | Crash fix prompts |

## 8. Runtime / Tooling Preferences

### Rust

- Channel: `1.95.0` (from `rust-toolchain.toml`)
- Profile: `minimal`
- Components: `rustfmt`, `clippy`, `rust-analyzer`, `rust-src`
- Targets:
  - `aarch64-linux-android` — Android port
  - `wasm32-wasip2` — extensions
  - `wasm32-unknown-unknown` — GPUI on the web
  - `x86_64-unknown-linux-musl` — remote server

### Build Caching

- `sccache` v0.10.0 with Cloudflare R2 (configured via `script/setup-sccache`)
- `.cargo/config.toml`: v0 symbol mangling for better backtraces, `tokio_unstable` feature

### Formatters

- `rustfmt` (edition 2024, style_edition 2024)
- `prettier` (printWidth 120 for code)
- Full lint suite: `./script/clippy`, `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, `./script/prettier`, `typos`

### CI

- Generated by `cargo xtask workflows` using the `gh-workflow` crate
- No `.github/workflows/` committed — CI lives externally
- `./script/clippy` is preferred over `cargo clippy` (it passes `--workspace`, `--release`, `--all-targets`, `--all-features`, `--deny warnings`)
- Linux docker-based builds via `script/install-linux` and `script/bundle-linux`

## 9. Testing & QA

### Test Frameworks

- **`#[gpui::test]`**: Custom proc-macro for async tests with GPUI lifecycle. Features: seed control, iterations, retries, failure reporting. Test functions receive `&mut TestAppContext`. Runs in GPUI's foreground executor.
- **`#[gpui::property_test]`**: Property-based testing variant based on proptest. Supports `Arbitrary`-derived strategies, custom `#[strategy = ...]` annotations, and GPUI context parameters. Uses `.no_shrink()` for scheduler seeds.
- **`#[test]`**: Standard Rust `#[test]` for pure logic without GPUI dependencies.

### Test-Runner Commands

- CI: `cargo nextest run --workspace --no-fail-fast`
- Local: `cargo test --workspace`

### Gate Patterns

- `#[cfg(feature = "test-support")]` — test-only helper code compiled into the crate
- `#[cfg(test)]` — inline test modules (standard)

### Key Test Helpers

- `FakeFs` — in-memory filesystem for tests
- `FakeHttpClient` — mock HTTP client
- `FakeLanguageModel` — mock language model
- `Project::test()` — test-harness project factory
- `SettingsStore::test()` — test-harness settings
- `VisualTestContext` — window-aware test context
- `cx.background_executor().timer(duration).await` — GPUI-aware timers

### Environment Variables

- `ITERATIONS` — override test iterations
- `SEED` — deterministic seed for PRNG-dependent tests
- `RUST_LOG` — logging level for test output

### Fixture Data

- Marked text with Unicode markers for cursor/selection positions
- JSON file trees for worktree/project test scenarios

### Typical Test Pattern

```rust
#[gpui::test]
async fn test_something(mut cx: &mut TestAppContext) {
    init_test(&cx);                               // setup logging, settings, etc.
    let fs = FakeFs::new(cx.background_executor().clone());
    let project = Project::test(fs, &[], &cx).await;
    // ... operate ...
    cx.run_until_parked();                        // advance GPUI scheduler
    // ... assert ...
}
```

## 10. Rules Hygiene

See `.rules` for the complete guidelines on maintaining agent rules.

Key principles:
- Rules are for **traps to avoid**, not maps to follow
- High bar for new rules: non-obvious, repeatedly encountered, and specific enough to act on
- After any agentic session, include a "Suggested .rules additions" heading in PR description with proposed text
- Do not edit `.rules` inline during normal feature/fix work
- Single-crate rules belong in that crate's own `.rules` file
- Avoid architectural descriptions in rules (they go stale fast)
